<http://data.silknow.org/object/930996f4-ad3a-3afc-92a4-990dedc37899/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Silk programme on cream silk in black typography, with right and left hand sides roughly cut and frayed to form slight minimal fringe, featuring a royal crest, centre top, surrounded by the words Theatre Royal.  Featuring the date, details of the benefit, and the list of characters in the plays to be performed, <i>Gilderoy, or, The Reiver Converted</i>, and J.B. Buckstone's melodrama <i>Presumptive Evidence, or, Murder Will Out</i>, 12 January 1835. The playbill notes that a Nautical Hornpipe and a Highland Fling will be performed, and that men from the 24th Regiment, from the Garrison, will perform as Soldiers, Highlanders, Countrymen and other, in the drama <i>Gilderoy</i>."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/930996f4-ad3a-3afc-92a4-990dedc37899> .

